<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{@invoice.invoice_number}</title>

    <%!-- The same stylesheet the on-screen document uses, in `:print` mode so
    it also carries the paper rules. This page deliberately loads none of
    `app.css`: its mask-based icon classes and daisyUI theme are not available
    to a saved file, and an icon rendered through them came out blank. --%>
    <Renderer.stylesheet doc={@doc} mode={:print} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Renderer.document doc={@doc} invoice={@invoice} accent={@accent} logo={@logo} />
    <%!-- A raw script rather than a colocated hook: this is a controller-
    rendered page with no LiveSocket, so there is no hook to colocate onto.

    Nonced like the one in the root layout. This page renders with the layout
    switched off, so it does not inherit that tag — and without the nonce the
    Content-Security-Policy blocks this, which does not fail loudly: the page
    renders perfectly and simply never opens the print dialog. --%>
    <script nonce={@conn.assigns[:csp_nonce]}>
      // Straight into the print dialog, where "Save as PDF" writes the file.
      window.addEventListener("load", () => window.print())
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
